Perpendicular Desktop
Copyright 2026 Perpendicular Desktop contributors

An independent desktop virtualization project for Windows 11 ARM on Apple Silicon.
Parallels Desktop is used as a behavioral reference. This project is not affiliated
with Parallels and does not include its binaries, Windows installation media,
license checks, guest tools, or copied decompiled source code.

The project's original source is provided under Apache License 2.0. Runtime
dependencies keep their respective licenses. The bundled bootstrap runtime uses
QEMU, TianoCore EDK II firmware, swtpm/libtpms and their dependency libraries.
Build tooling must preserve those packages' notices and source provenance.

QEMU source and corresponding license:
https://download.qemu.org/qemu-11.1.2.tar.xz
https://www.qemu.org/docs/master/about/license.html

The optional adaptive-display runtime applies the GPLv2 QEMU patches retained
in experimental/runtime-display. Its 2D RAMFB/VirtIO wrapper is adapted from the
UTM QEMU fork at 88e5ee7ec6703662fec7b638cca74c4769e683d6:
https://github.com/utmapp/qemu/tree/88e5ee7ec6703662fec7b638cca74c4769e683d6
The applied patches, source/dependency provenance and notices accompany that
modified binary in ThirdPartyNotices/PerpendicularRuntime. No Parallels code is
used by that runtime.

Secure firmware source (also included in the pinned QEMU source archive):
https://github.com/tianocore/edk2

Optional offline variable-enrollment build tool (GPL-2.0-only, not linked into
the app); its notices and public certificate provenance are retained:
https://gitlab.com/kraxel/virt-firmware
https://github.com/microsoft/secureboot_objects

TPM emulation:
https://github.com/stefanberger/swtpm
https://github.com/stefanberger/libtpms

Independently distributed Windows guest drivers/tools (optional):
